  "slug": "graph-attention-90e2",
  "summary": "Cellular transcriptional profiles and cross-modal encoder fusion are now supplying supervision beyond molecular structure for drug discovery models.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is learned molecular representations built by combining encoders across modalities. DCI-SiteDTA and ResGIN-Att use attention to integrate residue, graph, and cell-line information for affinity and synergy prediction, and the multi-target design method fuses target protein sequence embeddings into latent vectors for ligand generation. What is new is supervision beyond molecular structure: CellChem pretrains molecular embeddings on large-scale cellular transcriptional profiles, and the HDAC study applies a GNN-Transformer to LINCS L1000 signatures across more than 28,000 compounds. Not all items share this thread; the HDAC study is primarily a screening application rather than a representation-design contribution.",
